$ satlink at --help
exit status 0
--- stdout
Send a raw AT command, e.g. `satlink at AT+CSQ`

Usage: satlink at [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Arguments:
  <COMMAND>
          AT command to send, such as AT+CSQ

Options:
  -p, --port <PORT>
          Serial device (auto-detected by USB vendor ID when omitted)
          
          [env: SATLINK_PORT=]

  -t, --timeout <TIMEOUT>
          Seconds to wait for the final result
          
          [default: 10]

  -b, --baud <BAUD>
          Serial port speed, in bits per second
          
          [default: 19200]

      --simulate[=<SIMULATE>]
          Use a simulated handset instead of a real one, with Iridium's real timing (the default) or instant responses

          Possible values:
          - iridium: Call setup, latency and throughput as measured on Iridium
          - instant: No delays: for quick experiments

  -v, --verbose...
          Log what the link is doing (-v), in more detail (-vv, -vvv)

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
--- stderr
